  "answer": "This has been reported before. New+ only shows up in the Windows 11 modern context menu. When the classic menu is forced with the {86ca1aa0-34aa-4e8b-a509-50c905bae2a2} registry key, it doesn't appear on the folder background, even though the win10 shell extension DLL loads (PowerToys#48512). Other PowerToys extensions are affected the same way (PowerToys#47575). The archive has no fix. The only confirmed workaround is to delete that registry key and restart Explorer, which brings back the modern menu where New+ works. A few users on PowerToys#35312 reported it started working after a reboot or hibernate. Others recommend this reset, though it did not help in PowerToys#48512: turn New+ off, run Remove-AppxPackage on the Microsoft.PowerToys.NewPlusContextMenu package, turn New+ back on, then restart Explorer. Classic-menu support for New+ is being tracked as a feature request."
 },
